{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"externalID":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift#L91"}},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with one of the factories, which fill in the endpoint, the credentials’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header field, this encoder and its limits:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one member, ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an array","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of track calls, one per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, in the spec’s field names (below), and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":", in RudderStack’s calls alone"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, in UTC"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"track\""}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call, no traits,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and no ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". An endpoint counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its anonymous users are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is its own anonymous user, linked to nothing: the spec rejects a call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with neither a ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nor an ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its session, so it goes out with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its first send. Segment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deduplicates calls by ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over about the last 24 hours, and drops most duplicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than all, so a recovered record Segment had already stored before the app ended is most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s references don’t say whether they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deduplicate. The record’s vendor identifier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in every call, which the spec reads as the user’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Segment records no address from the request. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" member from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the request unless the call has one, even when ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is set, and passes it on to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Customer.io’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes the place of the address it reads from an HTTP","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. No call to Segment or Customer.io carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which their specs don’t have.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"sentAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"originalTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"channel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent. Without ","type":"text"},{"code":"sentAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the endpoint takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it is, uncorrected for the device’s clock; it is left out on purpose, as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retried request sends the same body again, whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"sentAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would be the first attempt’s.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"RudderStack, whose references list all three as required, fills them in from when it received","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the call.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"text":" holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"namespace"},{"text":", the bundle identifier, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"},{"text":", each left out when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":"; no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"text":" when all three are","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the platform as Segment’s Swift library names it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"ios","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a phone or pad, ","type":"text"},{"code":"macos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tvos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"watchos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"visionos","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"cellular","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whether the connection is each","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name is one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices, one whose event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and one too large for a call ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifi